WEBVTT

00:02.717 --> 00:06.846
I've already
implemented my tactics.

00:09.182 --> 00:10.266
What?!

00:25.198 --> 00:29.118
Okuyasu's brother almost
did me in back there.

00:29.828 --> 00:32.914
Koichi, I think it's time
we hightail it out of here.

00:33.123 --> 00:33.873
Huh?

00:34.082 --> 00:37.293
But what about the bow and
arrow that got me?

00:37.502 --> 00:38.711
The bow and arrow?

00:38.962 --> 00:41.965
Okuyasu's brother must've
hid it somewhere.

00:42.298 --> 00:43.757
Don't tell me you…?

00:44.009 --> 00:44.801
Yes…

00:45.093 --> 00:46.636
Don't forget…

00:46.720 --> 00:50.140
They said their dad's
around here somewhere.

00:50.724 --> 00:54.853
Look, I'm hurt pretty bad.
Let's just leave it be for now.

00:54.936 --> 00:56.938
W-We can't do that!

00:57.897 --> 01:02.397
I-I'm alive today cause
you healed my wounds, but…

01:03.319 --> 01:05.821
If someone else is shot
with that bow and arrow,

01:05.947 --> 01:07.990
they won't be so lucky!

01:08.199 --> 01:09.575
Another will die in Morioh!

01:11.202 --> 01:12.828
You can stay here.

01:13.204 --> 01:15.748
I can go find it by myself!

01:17.333 --> 01:21.833
Besides, I don't think
their dad is in this house anymore.

01:23.173 --> 01:27.177
I-If he was,
he would've come out by now.

01:30.472 --> 01:34.100
<i>He doesn't look it,
but he's got a helluva lot of guts.</i>

01:34.559 --> 01:36.143
<i>At least when
the going gets tough…</i>

01:36.227 --> 01:37.686
<i>Or when he's not thinking.</i>

01:37.854 --> 01:39.397
<i>Whatever the case,</i>

01:39.481 --> 01:42.859
<i>we better get
the hell out of this place fast.</i>

01:47.363 --> 01:48.072
Hey…

01:48.156 --> 01:50.867
W-What?
You're not stopping me.

01:51.076 --> 01:52.202
I'm not.

01:52.410 --> 01:54.620
We're gonna snap that
bow and arrow in two,

01:54.704 --> 01:56.372
then say goodbye to
this dump together,

01:56.790 --> 01:57.624
Koichi.

02:26.528 --> 02:28.821
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

02:30.031 --> 02:33.325
<i>These faceless gazes pass by one another</i>

02:33.701 --> 02:36.995
<i>A wound to the heart changes our everyday</i>

02:37.205 --> 02:41.705
<i>Encounters without boundaries
The bizarre is our normal U-yeh</i>

02:44.254 --> 02:47.757
<i>These ordinary mornings,
we're laughing on the surface</i>

02:47.882 --> 02:51.218
<i>Mysteries drawn to each other,
identity still unknown</i>

02:51.302 --> 02:55.802
<i>Without a heads up,
it's quietly lurking somewhere in this town</i>

03:00.562 --> 03:05.062
<i>Although we bicker and complain
In the end, we celebrate</i>

03:07.569 --> 03:10.947
<i>Dancing through the everyday</i>

03:11.030 --> 03:15.530
<i>Crazy Noisy Bizarre Town</i>

03:28.381 --> 03:32.676
EPISODE 5
THE NIJIMURA BROTHERS, PART 3

03:31.593 --> 03:32.698
There's an attic.

03:33.261 --> 03:34.637
The bow and arrow's
probably up here.

03:45.106 --> 03:46.398
Th-There it is!

03:46.524 --> 03:47.483
The bow and arrow!

03:47.609 --> 03:49.110
It's on the wall back there!

03:57.285 --> 04:01.205
Hey, this doesn't sound good.
Something's in there.

04:04.918 --> 04:07.211
Something
chained up in there?

04:07.378 --> 04:08.837
Maybe it's a dog?

04:08.922 --> 04:11.382
That's definitely not
a person in there…

04:13.801 --> 04:15.385
It sounds like
some kind of animal.

04:27.982 --> 04:30.359
This is really scary!
What do we do now?!

04:30.526 --> 04:31.902
What do we do now?

04:32.111 --> 04:33.529
This was all your idea!

04:33.655 --> 04:34.989
I know, but…

04:35.490 --> 04:37.033
We can't go back now.

04:37.242 --> 04:38.076
All right, Koichi.

04:38.243 --> 04:41.704
On the count of three,
you bust the door open.

04:41.788 --> 04:43.206
That should scare it.

04:43.539 --> 04:46.750
Then I'll run over and break
the bow and arrow in half.

04:46.918 --> 04:47.793
Got it?

04:48.753 --> 04:49.712
Yeah.

04:53.299 --> 04:54.341
Let's do this.

04:56.427 --> 04:57.302
One…

04:57.720 --> 04:58.470
Two…

04:58.846 --> 04:59.596
Three!

05:03.017 --> 05:04.351
What the hell?!

05:05.061 --> 05:05.853
Koichi!

05:08.189 --> 05:09.315
Help!

05:09.399 --> 05:11.984
That's no Stand.
That's a real hand!

05:12.151 --> 05:14.069
That's a real arm!

05:14.529 --> 05:16.739
H-Help me!

05:21.202 --> 05:22.870
Gross…

05:23.288 --> 05:25.248
I wasn't trying to sever it…

05:59.282 --> 06:01.784
Wh-What the heck was that?

06:01.993 --> 06:05.413
To think it's been living
in my own backyard…

06:05.538 --> 06:07.081
Gah…

06:07.248 --> 06:09.250
So you finally saw him…

06:09.334 --> 06:11.419
You were never
supposed to see him!

06:14.589 --> 06:15.965
You again…

06:18.426 --> 06:22.926
You're looking at…
our father.

06:24.557 --> 06:28.143
And Dad needs these.

06:30.104 --> 06:31.980
Th-The bow and arrow…

06:33.274 --> 06:36.694
I must find more Stand users
for Dad.

06:36.944 --> 06:38.987
That's why I'll never

06:39.197 --> 06:41.365
let anyone have them.

06:41.616 --> 06:43.534
I'll protect them forever!

06:44.410 --> 06:46.036
Did some disease
do this to him?

06:46.162 --> 06:48.122
A disease?
Not even close.

06:48.206 --> 06:51.000
Dad's in excellent health,

06:51.292 --> 06:53.168
with a hearty appetite.

06:54.128 --> 06:56.380
All he does is moan.

06:56.464 --> 06:58.924
You can bet he has
no awareness I'm his son.

06:59.425 --> 07:01.802
So you've been searching for
a Stand user

07:01.886 --> 07:03.012
who can cure your father.

07:03.304 --> 07:04.513
Cure?

07:05.848 --> 07:09.184
You mean you cure him?
Wrong again, I'm afraid.

07:15.650 --> 07:16.609
Completely wrong!

07:17.068 --> 07:21.568
I've been searching for
a Stand user who'll kill Dad.

07:23.533 --> 07:25.952
Dad won't die.
He can't die!

07:26.160 --> 07:27.661
I could bash his head in,

07:27.995 --> 07:31.498
chop him into tiny pieces,
slice him to ribbons,

07:31.582 --> 07:32.874
and he'd never die!

07:36.462 --> 07:38.922
He deserves the right to die.

07:39.340 --> 07:43.302
I swore, ever since I was a child,
I'd do anything to give him that.

07:43.845 --> 07:47.139
To do that,
I need the bow and arrow.

07:47.932 --> 07:52.432
Without it, Dad will go on
like this for all eternity.

07:52.687 --> 07:56.273
All because some bastard named
DIO decided to implant his cells

07:56.357 --> 07:59.818
inside his skull and turn him
into a monster!

08:00.027 --> 08:02.320
DIO?
Did you say DIO?

08:02.697 --> 08:04.990
That the same guy
Mr. Jotaro was talking about?

08:07.201 --> 08:10.495
Let me tell you a bit
about what used to be,

08:11.122 --> 08:12.665
Josuke Higashikata.

08:13.708 --> 08:18.208
What I'm about to tell you
isn't completely unrelated to your life.

08:19.589 --> 08:24.089
It all started eleven years ago,
in 1988.

08:25.553 --> 08:28.847
I was seven,
Okuyasu was four.

08:30.099 --> 08:32.309
We were living in Tokyo.

08:32.768 --> 08:34.311
It was the middle of
the Bubble Economy,

08:34.395 --> 08:35.938
and spirits were high,

08:36.147 --> 08:39.525
except my father's.

08:40.359 --> 08:42.069
Mom grew sick and died,

08:42.320 --> 08:44.447
and Dad's business
went under.

08:43.738 --> 08:48.117
LUXURY CONDOMINIUMS
NIJIMURA PROPERTIES CO.

08:44.572 --> 08:46.657
He was buried under
a mountain of debt.

08:51.412 --> 08:54.206
He'd often beat us
for no apparent reason.

08:54.457 --> 08:56.959
Dad was
the consummate loser.

08:59.128 --> 09:00.838
Then, suddenly,

09:02.507 --> 09:06.135
seemingly endless wads of cash
started rolling in.

09:06.761 --> 09:10.097
There were even jewels
and precious metals.

09:10.431 --> 09:12.808
But Dad didn't have a job.

09:14.769 --> 09:17.188
It was only later, after
some research, that I found out.

09:17.438 --> 09:21.938
My own father had sold
his soul to DIO.

09:22.860 --> 09:25.779
He became one of his lackeys
for monetary gain.

09:27.949 --> 09:32.449
Apparently DIO was scouring
the globe for potential Stand users.

09:33.663 --> 09:38.000
Somehow, he figured out
Dad was Stand-capable,

09:38.626 --> 09:43.005
though, to this day, I have no idea
what his Stand is.

09:43.506 --> 09:45.174
Then one day…

09:45.424 --> 09:47.217
It was ten years ago,

09:47.301 --> 09:49.136
but I remember it
like it was yesterday.

09:51.138 --> 09:53.223
It was 2 in the afternoon,

09:53.307 --> 09:55.434
and I'd just come home
from school…

09:57.019 --> 09:58.145
<i>Okuyasu!</i>

09:59.564 --> 10:03.401
<i>Did he hit you again?
That bastard!</i>

10:03.568 --> 10:05.111
<i>N-No!</i>

10:05.319 --> 10:06.069
<i>Huh?</i>

10:10.491 --> 10:11.366
<i>DIO…</i>

10:12.326 --> 10:13.702
<i>DIO's died…</i>

10:14.662 --> 10:16.413
<i>That must be the reason!</i>

10:17.665 --> 10:18.624
<i>Dad?</i>

10:22.211 --> 10:24.713
<i>Dad, I'll Callan ambulance.</i>

10:24.797 --> 10:27.382
<i>It's no use! I'm not sick!</i>

10:27.508 --> 10:30.219
<i>The flesh bud's
ravaging my body!</i>

10:30.344 --> 10:33.722
<i>— This is the end!
— Dad!</i>

10:34.348 --> 10:36.433
In the span of one year,

10:36.517 --> 10:38.977
he had lost his ability
to recognize us,

10:39.186 --> 10:41.313
and had become a
muttering glob of flesh!

10:43.733 --> 10:48.233
DIO implanted his own cells into
the minds of those he distrusted,

10:49.947 --> 10:52.074
enabling him to manipulate
his victims at will.

10:52.533 --> 10:56.245
DIO implanted
one of those things in Dad!

10:59.373 --> 11:02.209
For ten years I threw myself
into research.

11:02.460 --> 11:05.337
I studied Stands,
I learned about Jotaro…

11:05.880 --> 11:08.424
Then I learned of
Enyaba the hag,

11:08.591 --> 11:10.968
and got a hold of
the bow and arrow.

11:11.552 --> 11:13.637
But in the process,

11:13.804 --> 11:16.139
I resigned myself to
the fact that

11:16.223 --> 11:18.308
Dad would never recover.

11:19.185 --> 11:23.022
He had become one with
DIO's immortal cells.

11:23.648 --> 11:25.691
He spends his days
doing nothing but this.

11:25.983 --> 11:27.985
Every cursed day…

11:28.361 --> 11:30.488
Every moment of every day,
for the past ten years,

11:30.863 --> 11:34.616
he's desperately scratched
around that box of rubbish.

11:34.867 --> 11:38.829
Dare I confiscate the box,
he wails and groans for days.

11:39.121 --> 11:40.455
I'm sick of it all!

11:40.748 --> 11:42.499
I look at him,

11:42.583 --> 11:45.544
and I become disgusted with
the idea of life itself.

11:47.588 --> 11:51.091
I've told you over and over,
stop making this blasted mess!

11:54.679 --> 11:59.179
When I discipline him,
the bastard seems to hear me!

11:59.684 --> 12:01.686
Yet the rummaging
continues…

12:01.769 --> 12:04.104
The wretched swine
can't help himself!

12:05.064 --> 12:06.148
Bleh…

12:06.607 --> 12:08.817
Hey! The only one who needs
to stop is you!

12:08.943 --> 12:10.986
He's still your father!

12:13.447 --> 12:14.656
In a way you're right.

12:14.865 --> 12:17.659
He is my father…
my blood.

12:18.160 --> 12:21.997
But the father I see
before me isn't the father I know.

12:22.665 --> 12:24.750
This man sold
his soul to DIO.

12:24.834 --> 12:26.627
This man is living
the life he created!

12:27.837 --> 12:29.421
At the same time,

12:30.131 --> 12:33.092
seeing my own father like
this is unbearable.

12:33.634 --> 12:35.427
Do you have any idea
how this feels?

12:35.803 --> 12:40.182
That's why I want to give him
the chance to die.

12:41.600 --> 12:45.812
With him dead,
I'll finally be able to live again!

12:53.821 --> 12:56.907
Goddammit!
I told you to stop!

12:57.158 --> 12:58.576
I'm sick of all this!

12:59.618 --> 13:00.368
Hey!

13:00.828 --> 13:02.704
That's enough!

13:03.038 --> 13:05.707
Sorry, but I can't let
you have this bow and arrow.

13:06.292 --> 13:07.334
Not now, not ever!

13:07.543 --> 13:09.044
You seem to be mistaken!

13:09.295 --> 13:11.422
I'll get the bow and arrow later.

13:12.965 --> 13:15.884
My sights are on that box!

13:17.887 --> 13:18.888
Th-The box?

13:31.275 --> 13:34.444
The way he's been
clutching those scraps of paper,

13:34.570 --> 13:36.488
there's something there.

13:37.448 --> 13:38.907
It all makes sense now.

13:47.875 --> 13:49.585
A family photo…

13:50.711 --> 13:52.295
He knew what he was doing.

13:52.463 --> 13:56.425
For ten years
he had a purpose.

13:56.717 --> 14:00.053
He was looking for the photo
of his sons when they were young.

14:01.639 --> 14:04.099
He may not be
completely aware,

14:04.391 --> 14:07.811
but deep down in his heart,
he has his memories!

14:08.270 --> 14:09.604
Memories of
a time long past!

14:29.708 --> 14:31.459
THE HAND

14:43.097 --> 14:45.057
If you can give up on
a Stand that kills,

14:45.641 --> 14:48.393
in favor of a
Stand that heals,

14:50.020 --> 14:51.646
then I'm willing to help.

14:55.067 --> 14:57.611
But you'll have to hand over
that bow and arrow.

14:57.820 --> 14:59.154
I'm gonna break 'em in two.

15:03.492 --> 15:05.160
Planning on running?

15:07.872 --> 15:10.958
Bro, please,
stop this.

15:11.458 --> 15:13.001
Okuyasu!

15:13.127 --> 15:17.627
Come on, let's just put
an end to all this, okay?

15:18.465 --> 15:19.674
So you were here…

15:21.176 --> 15:24.554
There's a chance
Dad could get better, right?

15:26.974 --> 15:30.102
So what if he doesn't look
like he used to.

15:30.436 --> 15:34.936
He could have his soul back,
his memories.

15:36.150 --> 15:37.359
Right?

15:42.448 --> 15:45.200
Okuyasu! What do you think
you're doing?

15:45.659 --> 15:47.035
Bro…

15:47.870 --> 15:49.496
Out of my way, Okuyasu!

15:49.580 --> 15:53.542
No matter what happens,
I can never turn back!

15:53.667 --> 15:55.126
With this very
bow and arrow,

15:55.210 --> 15:58.338
I've already slaughtered
countless people in this town!

15:58.839 --> 16:02.634
Besides, to me,
you're no longer my brother!

16:02.843 --> 16:04.219
You're no longer my brother,

16:04.303 --> 16:06.555
which is why I can kill you
without a second thought!

16:09.183 --> 16:11.059
<i>Bro…</i>

16:18.484 --> 16:19.443
Quick question…

16:19.693 --> 16:22.946
Anyone else in your family
besides you two and your dad?

16:23.530 --> 16:27.033
Anyone else?
It's just the three of us.

16:35.209 --> 16:36.335
Th-That's…

16:36.877 --> 16:38.587
<i>It's coming from the outlet…</i>

16:39.004 --> 16:40.005
Okuyasu!

16:40.172 --> 16:42.424
Pull your head out of your ass,
you idiot!

16:45.678 --> 16:46.804
Bro!

16:47.888 --> 16:51.808
I'll be taking this bow and
arrow, Keicho Nijimura!

16:51.892 --> 16:53.101
Remember me?

16:53.185 --> 16:55.604
You were kind enough
to shoot me with this arrow

16:55.688 --> 16:57.439
and awaken my Stand!

16:58.148 --> 16:59.649
You…

16:59.775 --> 17:02.611
You think you can handle
this bow and arrow?

17:02.736 --> 17:04.320
Keicho Nijimura!

17:04.405 --> 17:06.698
You said Stands are a
manifestation of the soul, correct?

17:06.865 --> 17:08.700
Well, I've matured!

17:09.118 --> 17:12.663
Or did you not expect my Stand,
Chili Pepper,

17:12.746 --> 17:15.165
to have come this far?

17:15.416 --> 17:17.042
Worse Company!

17:17.126 --> 17:18.794
Stop talking!

17:19.795 --> 17:20.587
Th-That's…

17:20.713 --> 17:21.630
Electricity!

17:21.714 --> 17:24.508
Okuyasu's brother's turning
into electricity!

17:24.633 --> 17:25.967
And so is
the bow and arrow!

17:26.135 --> 17:26.969
Bro!

17:27.344 --> 17:29.346
Get away from me!

17:29.847 --> 17:33.517
You'll be pulled in, too!

17:34.018 --> 17:35.310
Bro…

17:35.894 --> 17:37.145
S-Shit!

17:37.229 --> 17:40.815
He's taking
the bow and arrow!

17:41.108 --> 17:42.317
Okuyasu…

17:42.943 --> 17:47.443
You… You've always
held me back!

17:51.618 --> 17:53.286
Bro!

17:57.458 --> 17:58.542
Josuke!

18:04.965 --> 18:06.716
<i>Without a doubt a Stand user</i>

18:06.800 --> 18:09.010
<i>was pee ring in
from that window</i>

18:10.095 --> 18:12.722
That Stand back there…
do you know it, Okuyasu?

18:13.474 --> 18:17.974
N-No. Bro didn't tell me about
a lot of the Stand users he found.

18:21.482 --> 18:23.025
J-Josuke!

18:23.108 --> 18:24.984
Th-That's…

18:37.664 --> 18:39.165
Okuyasu…

18:40.084 --> 18:44.129
Bro…
it was only a matter of time.

18:44.922 --> 18:47.382
I knew he'd do
bad things with his life.

18:47.508 --> 18:49.343
It was his fate.

18:49.635 --> 18:50.719
But…

18:51.512 --> 18:53.764
But in the end, Bro…

18:53.931 --> 18:56.141
My brother, in the end,
at the very last second,

18:56.225 --> 18:58.435
he saved me,
didn't he?

18:58.602 --> 19:01.521
Josuke,
you saw it, right?

19:02.231 --> 19:04.691
Yeah.
Without a doubt.

19:05.359 --> 19:08.904
Your brother
saved your life.

19:30.926 --> 19:33.553
<i>Is this Jotaro Kujo?</i>

19:35.347 --> 19:36.765
I don't recognize your voice.

19:36.890 --> 19:38.600
Who is this?

19:38.851 --> 19:40.269
<i>Who I am doesn't matter.</i>

19:40.811 --> 19:42.479
<i>Jotaro Kujo,</i>

19:42.563 --> 19:46.441
<i>I'm asking you kindly
to get the hell out of Morioh.</i>

19:47.025 --> 19:48.943
Let me see
if I've got this straight,

19:49.153 --> 19:52.364
a complete stranger wants me
to leave town for no particular reason.

19:52.573 --> 19:54.992
If you were me,
would you get up and leave?

19:55.075 --> 19:57.744
<i>I have the bow and arrow</i>

19:58.912 --> 20:03.082
<i>I took it…
after I killed Keicho Nijimura.</i>

20:03.417 --> 20:05.460
<i>And I don't mind
getting rid of you either.</i>

20:05.544 --> 20:07.212
<i>You know I've heard Jotaro…</i>

20:07.421 --> 20:11.466
<i>you have the ability to stop
time for one or two seconds.</i>

20:11.842 --> 20:13.969
<i>But since you're
such a tough guy,</i>

20:14.136 --> 20:16.888
<i>I thought I'd try to convince
you over the phone first.</i>

20:17.139 --> 20:18.974
Are you a Stand user too?

20:19.308 --> 20:21.143
What do you want
with the bow and arrow?

20:21.351 --> 20:24.479
<i>I don't mean to
cause you any trouble.</i>

20:24.605 --> 20:29.105
NUMBER WITHHELD PUBLIC PHONE

20:24.938 --> 20:28.024
<i>As long as Josuke Higashikata
minds his own business,</i>

20:28.525 --> 20:30.006
<i>I won't lay
a finger on him, either.</i>

20:30.527 --> 20:33.655
<i>I just received
this Stand ability.</i>

20:33.822 --> 20:36.741
<i>All I want is
to have a little fun.</i>

20:36.909 --> 20:41.288
<i>I've had enough
entrance exams and resumes.</i>

20:41.788 --> 20:42.914
So you're a student?

20:43.498 --> 20:45.291
<i>What the hell difference
does that make?!</i>

20:45.375 --> 20:48.711
<i>Listen! If you wear out
your welcome in my town,</i>

20:49.129 --> 20:50.255
<i>I'll kill both you and Josuke!
Got it?!</i>

20:50.339 --> 20:52.507
How many other Stand users
are in this—

21:08.649 --> 21:10.025
Good grief…

21:12.361 --> 21:13.862
<i>Keicho Nijimura was buried</i>

21:13.946 --> 21:17.699
<i>in Kunimi Peak Cemetery,
west of Morioh.</i>

21:18.575 --> 21:22.203
<i>The bow and arrow
remains missing.</i>

21:18.992 --> 21:22.745
NIJIMURA FAMILY

21:23.163 --> 21:26.082
<i>For Okuyasu Nijimura,
it was time</i>

21:26.166 --> 21:28.585
<i>to keep his father company
for a while.</i>

21:28.919 --> 21:29.878
<i>And..</i>

21:34.174 --> 21:35.884
Josuke, can you get that?

21:38.470 --> 21:39.554
Okay…

21:40.847 --> 21:44.225
Hey, Josuke!
It's time to go to school!

21:44.476 --> 21:45.435
Huh?

21:45.519 --> 21:48.980
Starting today, I'm gonna be
going to the same school as you!

21:49.064 --> 21:51.524
That doesn't mean you
have to come and get me!

21:51.608 --> 21:53.901
This isn't
elementary school!

21:54.027 --> 21:58.281
Wow, I never knew your house
and my house were so close!

21:58.699 --> 22:01.451
Well, that is a surprise…

22:01.535 --> 22:03.537
Come on!
Let's go!

22:03.870 --> 22:05.872
Oh, so you're
Josuke's friend?

22:06.039 --> 22:08.499
Hi!
I'm Okuyasu Nijimura!

22:08.917 --> 22:11.502
Come in and have some coffee
while he gets ready.

22:11.878 --> 22:14.255
Really?
Don't mind if I do, then!

22:15.507 --> 22:17.592
You know,
your mom is really pretty.

22:17.926 --> 22:19.761
I'll be right there!

22:20.220 --> 22:24.515
Well, this is just great…
What'd I get myself into with this guy…?

23:38.882 --> 23:41.926
EPISODE 6
KOICHI HIROSE (REVERB)
